      "final_text": "Done. All 8 requirements verified.\n\nThe bug was the Proposal 62 start condition `recorded = 0 \u2227 index > compInitialIndex` in `distributeSupplierComp`/`distributeBorrowerComp`. When the upgrade set a never-rewarded market's index to exactly `compInitialIndex`, accounts with no recorded index were credited from 0 instead of `compInitialIndex`, minting `units` out of nothing.\n\nFix in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean): rewrote `CompRewards.comptroller` in the spec's closed form using `accrueSide`, `accrualStart` (with `compInitialIndex \u2264 index`), `creditFor`, `grant`, and the `SpeedsSet` update, as `if <preconditions> then some <next> else none` per call. The five effect/success theorems follow by `simp` + case split. The three bounds instantiate `ProofForgeFin.Accumulator.Market` (supply = side 1, borrow = side 2), prove both settlements, every `Op` as an `Act` via `exec_act`, read the upgrade as `Clock.reinit`, and apply `rewards_bounded`, `account_rewards_bounded`, and `rewards_after_no_position_bounded`.\n\n- `check_candidate`: `VERIFIED`, 8/8, 2001 property cases pass, six kernels accept.\n- Passport: `.proofforge/passport-001.json`, sha256 `304939394bd95b8442ed321352252a5edfa87a942eb636a5efb5e1132dc12765`.\n- `verify_passport`: reproduced.",
